creative block.

44
00:02:20.317 --> 00:02:22.305
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:22.605 --> 00:02:25.916
Have you seen the new installation at the exhibition hall?

46
00:02:27.217 --> 00:02:31.694
Yes! It's absolutely stunning. The choreographer performed there too.

47
00:02:32.983 --> 00:02:35.993
I found it fairly confusing at first, to be honest.

48
00:02:37.283 --> 00:02:41.062
Contemporary art can be quite challenging. The art critic loved it.

49
00:02:42.350 --> 00:02:46.105
I'm a bit stuck with my own writing. I've got creative block.

50
00:02:47.417 --> 00:02:50.731
Try a completely different activity. It really helps.

51
00:02:52.017 --> 00:02:55.793
Grammar focus: Adverbs of degree and extreme adjectives.

52
00:02:56.093 --> 00:03:00.193
Use absolutely or completely with extreme adjectives like stunning and awful.

53
00:03:00.493 --> 00:03:04.281
Use very, fairly or quite with normal adjectives like good and long.

54
00:03:04.581 --> 00:03:08.926
For example: The show was absolutely stunning, but the play was fairly long.

55
00:03:09.226 --> 00:03:14.093
Don't use very with extreme adjectives: say absolutely brilliant, not very brilliant.

56
00:03:15.083 --> 00:03:18.606
Now read and listen. A New Generation of Khmer Artists.

57
00:03:18.906 --> 00:03:21.835
Cambodia's contemporary art scene is growing quickly.

58
00:03:23.150 --> 00:03:27.390
Young painters, composers and playwrights are telling new stories about modern life.

59
00:03:28.683 --> 00:03:32.715
A choreographer in Phnom Penh mixes classical Apsara with hip-hop.

60
00:03:34.017 --> 00:03:37.166
Art critics say the results are absolutely fascinating.

61
00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:42.806
Exhibition halls and small galleries now host shows almost every weekend.

62
00:03:44.117 --> 00:03:46.618
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:46.918 --> 00:03:49.057
A person who writes plays is a blank.

64
00:03:49.357 --> 00:03:53.486
A, composer. B, playwright. C, choreographer.

65
00:03:57.483 --> 00:03:59.169
The answer is B: playwright.

66
00:04:00.683 --> 00:04:02.091
The view was blank amazing.

67
00:04:02.391 --> 00:04:05.533
A, very. B, absolutely. C, fairly.

68
00:04:09.550 --> 00:04:11.561
The answer is B: absolutely.

69
00:04:13.050 --> 00:04:15.735
The film was blank good, but not great.

70
00:04:16.035 --> 00:04:19.711
A, absolutely. B, fairly. C, completely.

71
00:04:23.717 --> 00:04:25.786
The answer is B: fairly.

72
00:04:27.283 --> 00:04:30.096
A time when you can't think of new ideas is blank.

73
00:04:30.396 --> 00:04:34.676
A, installation. B, creative block. C, contemporary.

74
00:04:38.683 --> 00:04:40.996
The answer is B: creative block.

75
00:04:42.483 --> 00:04:46.515
According to the text, the choreographer mixes Apsara with blank.

76
00:04:46.815 --> 00:04:50.898
A, ballet. B, hip-hop. C, folk dance.

77
00:04:54.883 --> 00:04:56.627
The answer is B: hip-hop.

78
00:04:58.117 --> 00:05:02.127
Now it's your turn to speak. Describe an artwork, film or show that impressed you.

79
00:05:07.427 --> 00:05:14.515
The light installation at the museum was absolutely breathtaking. I found it completely different from anything I'd seen.

80
00:05:14.815 --> 00:05:16.408
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:17.417 --> 00:05:22.646
Great work today! You learned eight new words and adverbs of degree and extreme adjectives.

82
00:05:22.946 --> 00:05:26.597
Today's value is creativity. Use your imagination when you play.

83
00:05:26.897 --> 00:05:30.397
See you in Unit twenty-three. Goodbye!

84
00:05:30.697 --> 00:05:33.407
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

